From fa9595e5d2c8e1d049ac613511e63bf9b668987d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:29:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add M5Stick K016 board

K016 is a classic ESP32-WROOM32 board with a 64x128 SH1107 monochrome
OLED on SPI (CS G14, DC G27, SCLK G18, MOSI G23), one custom button on
G35, blue LED G19, buzzer G26, IR G17, an MPU9250 nine-axis IMU (gray
version) at 0x68 and an IP5306 at 0x75 on a shared G21/G22 I2C bus.

- new machine m5stick and board glue, reusing the Basic v2.7 IP5306
  register model from 0113;
- new mono SH1107 mode for the generic SPI panel model: controller GDDRAM
  (128 columns x 16 pages), page/column addressing, display/segment/COM
  configuration commands, 64x128 console rendering and a raw GDDRAM QOM
  dump for offline analysis;
- new mpu9250 I2C model with WHO_AM_I 0x71, INT_STATUS data-ready and
  accel/gyro/temperature registers backed by QOM fixtures (no AK8963
  magnetometer model yet);
- fix the classic SPI panel sink to keep a TX snapshot for full-duplex
  DOUTDIN transactions (the RX copy used to overwrite the panel bytes);
- guard the classic I2C command engine against empty TX FIFOs instead of
  aborting the emulator on a malformed guest command list.

Wiring evidence: docs.m5stack.com/en/core/M5Stick PinMap, checked
2026-11-02.  The EasyLoader factory image boots the ROM/bootloader and app
but its legacy IDF I2C driver never presents FIFO data to the controller
model, so the MPU probe reports 0xFF and no factory-firmware button/IMU
data plane is claimed.
